A||N||6||2xsess||Speaker panel question||||5||
Z||000000||2xsess||09-14-2000||09:20 PM||||I have an 85GT and I want to put the 86-88 style rear speaker panels in it. My question is are there holes in the frame behind those speakers? I can't figure out how else to explain it.<BR>Thanks for your help,<BR>Jeff||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||09-15-2000||12:18 AM||||Hmmmm.....<P>I believe the answer is "yes."  If memory serves, think there is a cavity in the pillar to accomodate the speaker.  The speaker is attached to the pillar with screws, <B>if</B> I recall correctly.  <P>Sorry, all the interiors in my cars are more or less intact, so I'm not going to tear into them to find out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> !  Maybe one of the members has an "inwork" project car, and can answer your question.  Might even post a picture for you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">?  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||09-15-2000||02:48 AM||||No holes in the 84-85 Fiero's.  If you want them that bad you're gonna have to chop 'em out yourself.  <P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">    <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
Z||000003||2xsess||09-15-2000||04:33 AM||||So that's a defenite yes, there is holes in the frame? <P>So does anyone have an aternative way that I could put speakers in the rear. I don't really like the seat speakers, too close to my ears, when it hits a high it feels like my ears are going to burst. But I don't want to just have front speakers either.<P>Thanks,<BR>Jeff||||reg||1
Z||000004||whamel||09-15-2000||02:46 PM||||You could always just filter the highs out - it might be easier to just cap 'em off.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||myblack86GT||09-15-2000||05:06 PM||||Put some 6x9's behind the seats. Iv seen it done somewhere. Email sean@kdsi.net  I cant remember if it was his car or someone elses, but he might be able to help you out.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||09-15-2000||08:08 PM||||There are <B>NO</B> holes in the sail panels of the '84s and '85s.  I was originally planning to use the inner sail panels from the Monkeymobile ('86) in the Grape Ape, but decided that I didn't want to try cutting into the metal.  That's the only way to do it if you're going to use the stock panels as there is no clearance behind the plastic panels.||||reg||1
